# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# S3K CRM frontend configuration
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local      # .env.local is git-ignored
#
# Required for local development. The backend runs on port 8000 via
# `npm run dev:backend`, so this is the value that matches the repo's own
# start script.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000

# Leaving this unset means **same-origin** — the reverse-proxy topology doc 11
# assumes, where something in front of both serves the API under /api/v1 on the
# frontend's own host. It does not mean "no backend": running `next dev` with
# it unset produces an application whose every request 404s against the Next.js
# server, and a login screen that cannot sign anyone in.
#
# It has never meant "demo mode". An earlier revision did derive an AUTH_ENABLED
# flag from this value — a missing or misspelled variable then shipped an
# application with no login gate and every permission granted — and that switch
# was deliberately removed. A configuration mistake must not be able to widen
# access: see lib/api-config.ts.
#
# Only NEXT_PUBLIC_* values reach the browser. Never put a secret here.
